    dct:description "The correspondence between classification and descent is testable using independent evidence. The uniqueness and conceptual identity claims cannot be fully adjudicated by datasets." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Compare independently inferred molecular phylogenetic distances with historical and modern classifications and organismal similarity matrices. Stronger agreement with common descent than with non-genealogical similarity schemes supports the empirical content, but cannot establish the philosophical phrase 'only known cause.'" ;
